::before>\\n\\nTo help improve GitLab, we would like to periodically [ collect usage information ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md) . This can be changed at any time in [ your settings ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling#js-usage-settings) . \\n\\n[ Send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=1&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=1) [ Don\\'t send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=0&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=0)\\n\\n  1. <::after> [ Administrator  ](/root)\\n  2. <::after> [ docs-template-repo  ](/root/docs-template-repo)\\n  3. [ Repository Settings  ](/root/docs-template-repo/-/settings/repository)\\n\\n\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Branch defaults \\n\\nSelect the default branch for this project, and configure the template for branch names. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nDefault branch \\n\\nAll merge requests and commits are made against this branch unless you specify a different one. \\n\\nmain \\n\\nSelect default branch \\n\\n  * Branches  1 \\n  * main  default  protected \\n\\n\\n\\n1 result \\n\\n<::before><::after> Auto-close referenced issues on default branch \\n\\nWhen merge requests and commits in the default branch close, any issues they reference also close. [ ](/help/user/project/issues/managing_issues.md#closing-issues-automatically)\\n\\nBranch name template \\n\\nBranches created from issues follow this pattern. \\n\\nLeave empty to use default template. Maximum 255 characters. [ What variables can I use? ](/help/user/project/repository/branches/index.md#name-your-branch)\\n\\nSave changes \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nEdit branch protections, approval rules, and status checks from a single page. [ How to use branch rules? ](/help/user/project/repository/branches/branch_rules.md#create-a-branch-rule)\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Branch rules \\n\\nDefine rules for who can push, merge, and the required approvals for each branch. [ Leave feedback. ](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab/-/issues/388149)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Branch rules  1 \\n\\nAdd branch rule \\n\\n  * Branch name or pattern \\n\\n\\n\\n  * <::after>\\n\\n**main** default  protected \\n    * <::marker>Allowed to merge: 1 role \\n    * <::marker>Allowed to push and merge: 1 role \\n\\n[ View details  ](/root/docs-template-repo/-/settings/repository/branch_rules?branch=main)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Mirroring repositories \\n\\nSet up your project to automatically push and/or pull changes to/from another repository. Branches, tags, and commits will be synced automatically. [ How do I mirror repositories? ](/help/user/project/repository/mirror/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Mirrored repositories  0 \\n\\nAdd new \\n\\n####  Add new mirror repository \\n\\nGit repository URL \\n\\nThis field is required. \\n\\n  * The repository must be accessible over ` http:// ` , ` https:// ` , ` ssh:// ` or ` git:// ` . \\n  * When using the ` http:// ` or ` https:// ` protocols, please provide the exact URL to the repository. HTTP redirects will not be followed. \\n  * Do not include the username in the URL, use the username field below if required: ` https://gitlab.company.com/group/project.git ` . \\n  * When using the ` ssh:// ` protocol, please use the following format: ` ssh://username@example.com/group/project.git ` . \\n  * The update action will time out after 180 minutes. For big repositories, use a clone/push combination. \\n  * Pull mirrors will only create LFS objects if LFS is [ enabled for the project ](/help/topics/git/lfs/index.md) . \\n  * Push mirrors will only sync LFS objects if LFS is [ enabled for the project ](/help/topics/git/lfs/index.md) . \\n  * Push mirrors will **not** sync LFS objects over SSH. \\n  * In case of pull mirroring, your user will be the author of all events in the activity feed that are the result of an update, like new branches being created or new commits being pushed to existing branches. \\n\\n\\n\\nMirror direction \\n\\nPush \\n\\nLoading  Detect host keys \\n\\nFingerprints \\n\\nInput host keys manually  Hide host keys manual input \\n\\nSSH host keys \\n\\nThis field is required. \\n\\nAuthentication method  Username and Password  SSH public key \\n\\nUsername \\n\\nThis field is required. \\n\\nPassword \\n\\nThis field is required. \\n\\nKeep divergent refs \\n\\nDo not force push over diverged refs. After the mirror is created, this setting can only be modified using the API. [ Learn more about this option ](/help/user/project/repository/mirror/push.md#keep-divergent-refs) and [ the API. ](/help/api/remote_mirrors.md)\\n\\nMirror only protected branches \\n\\nIf enabled, only protected branches will be mirrored. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/repository/mirror/index.md#mirror-only-protected-branches)\\n\\nMirror repository  Cancel \\n\\nThere are currently no mirrored repositories. \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Protected branches \\n\\nKeep stable branches secure and force developers to use merge requests. [ What are protected branches? ](/help/user/project/repository/branches/protected.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nGiving merge rights to a protected branch also gives elevated permissions for certain CI/CD features. [ What are the security implications? ](/help/ci/pipelines/index.md#pipeline-security-on-protected-branches)\\n\\n##  Protected branches  1 \\n\\nBy default, protected branches restrict who can modify the branch. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/repository/branches/protected.md#who-can-modify-a-protected-branch)\\n\\nAdd protected branch \\n\\n####  Protect a branch \\n\\nBranch: \\n\\nSelect branch or create wildcard \\n\\n  * Create wildcard ` `\\n\\n\\n\\nLoading \\n\\n[ Wildcards ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/help/user/project/repository/branches/protected.md#protect-multiple-branches-with-wildcard-rules) such as ` *-stable ` or ` production/* ` are supported. [ Branch names are case-sensitive. ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/help/user/project/repository/branches/protected.md#branch-names-are-case-sensitive)\\n\\nAllowed to merge: \\n\\nSelect \\n\\n  * Roles \\n  * Developers + Maintainers \\n\\n  * Maintainers \\n\\n  * Instance admins \\n\\n  * No one \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAllowed to push and merge: \\n\\nSelect \\n\\n  * Roles \\n  * Developers + Maintainers \\n\\n  * Maintainers \\n\\n  * Instance admins \\n\\n  * No one \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nAllowed to force push: \\n\\nAllowed to force push \\n\\nAllow all users with push access to [ force push ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/help/topics/git/git_rebase.md#force-pushing) . \\n\\nProtect  Cancel \\n\\nBranch  |  Allowed to merge  |  Allowed to push and merge  |  Allowed to force push  |   \\n---|---|---|---|---  \\nmain  default  |  Maintainers \\n\\n  * Roles \\n  * Developers + Maintainers \\n  * Maintainers \\n  * Instance admins \\n  * No one \\n\\n|  Maintainers \\n\\n  * Roles \\n  * Developers + Maintainers \\n  * Maintainers \\n  * Instance admins \\n  * No one \\n\\n|  Toggle allowed to force push  |  [ Unprotect  ](/root/docs-template-repo/-/protected_branches/54?update_section=js-protected-branches-settings)  \\n  \\nExpand \\n\\n##  Protected tags \\n\\nLimit access to creating and updating tags. [ What are protected tags? ](/help/user/project/protected_tags.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nBy default, protected tags restrict who can modify the tag. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/protected_tags.md#who-can-modify-a-protected-tag)\\n\\n##  Protected tags  0 \\n\\nAdd tag \\n\\n####  Protect a tag \\n\\nTag \\n\\nSelect tag or create wildcard \\n\\n  * Create wildcard ` `\\n\\n\\n\\nLoading \\n\\n[ Wildcards ](/help/user/project/protected_tags.md#wildcard-protected-tags) such as ` v* ` or ` *-release ` are supported. \\n\\nAllowed to create \\n\\nSelect \\n\\n  * Roles \\n  * Developers + Maintainers \\n\\n  * Maintainers \\n\\n  * Instance admins \\n\\n  * No one \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nProtect  Cancel \\n\\nNo tags are protected. \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Deploy tokens \\n\\nDeploy tokens allow access to packages, your repository, and registry images. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Active deploy tokens  0 \\n\\nAdd token \\n\\n####  New deploy token \\n\\nCreate a new deploy token for all projects in this group. [ What are deploy tokens? ](/help/user/project/deploy_tokens/index.md)\\n\\nName \\n\\nEnter a unique name for your deploy token. Name the token gitlab-deploy-token to expose it to CI/CD jobs. \\n\\nExpiration date (optional) \\n\\nEnter an expiration date for your token. Defaults to never expire. \\n\\nUsername (optional) \\n\\nEnter a username for your token. Defaults to ` gitlab+deploy-token-{n} ` . \\n\\nScopes (select at least one) \\n\\nread_repository \\n\\nAllows read-only access to the repository. \\n\\nread_package_registry \\n\\nAllows read-only access to the package registry. \\n\\nwrite_package_registry \\n\\nAllows read, write and delete access to the package registry. \\n\\nCreate deploy token  Cancel \\n\\nThis project has no active deploy tokens. \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Deploy keys \\n\\nAdd deploy keys to grant read/write access to this repository. [ What are deploy keys? ](/help/user/project/deploy_keys/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Deploy keys \\n\\nAdd new key \\n\\n####  Add new deploy key \\n\\nTitle \\n\\nKey \\n\\nPaste a public key here. [ How do I generate it? ](/help/user/ssh.md)\\n\\nGrant write permissions to this key \\n\\nAllow this key to push to this repository \\n\\nExpiration date (optional) \\n\\nOptional but recommended. If set, key becomes invalid on the specified date. \\n\\nAdd key  Cancel \\n\\n<::after>\\n\\n<::after>\\n\\n  * <::before> Enabled deploy keys \\n  * <::before> Privately accessible deploy keys \\n  * <::before> Publicly accessible deploy keys \\n\\n\\n\\nNo deploy keys found, start by adding a new one above. \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Repository maintenance \\n\\nManage repository storage and cleanup. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nTo ensure that a full backup is available in case changes need to be restored, you should make an [ export of the project ](/help/user/project/settings/import_export.md) . \\n\\n#####  Remove blobs \\n\\nProvide a list of blob object IDs to be removed. [ How do I get a list of object IDs? ](/help/user/project/repository/repository_size.md#get-a-list-of-object-ids)\\n\\nAfterwards, run housekeeping manually to remove old versions of the file from Git history. \\n\\nRemove blobs \\n\\n#####  Redact text \\n\\nRedact known instances of text in the repository. The provided strings will be replaced with ` ***REMOVED*** ` . \\n\\nAfterwards, run housekeeping manually to remove old versions of the string from Git history. \\n\\nRedact text \\n\\n#####  Repository cleanup \\n\\nUpload a text file of objects, and then GitLab removes internal Git references to these objects. Use [ git filter-repo ](https://github.com/newren/git-filter-repo) on the repository to generate the list of objects to remove as a commit-map file. [ ](/help/user/project/repository/repository_size.md#repository-cleanup \"What happens during repository cleanup?\")\\n\\n######  Upload commit-map file \\n\\nChoose a file  No file selected \\n\\nThe maximum file size is 100 MiB. \\n\\nStart cleanup \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/docs-template-repo/-/settings/repository', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/docs-template-repo/-/settings/repository'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/docs-template-repo/-/settings/repository')\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='78'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"click('722')\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', 